{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4d9","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07916-2a5a-7c91-941e-599b9b859136"},"sequence":199,"recorded_at":1780531400000393,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"256d89a1-396a-4382-a1d7-c6813bb31cc7","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"256d89a1-396a-4382-a1d7-c6813bb31cc7","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"256d89a1-396a-4382-a1d7-c6813bb31cc7"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"2aa4973a-8890-4133-b2e6-715a44a0c4b0"},"task_id":"2aa4973a-8890-4133-b2e6-715a44a0c4b0","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"2aa4973a-8890-4133-b2e6-715a44a0c4b0","chunk":"Read text file `internal/provhost/refusal_arm_inventory_test.go`.\n1|package provhost\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"context\"\n5|\t\"encoding/json\"\n6|\t\"errors\"\n7|\t\"fmt\"\n8|\t\"go/ast\"\n9|\t\"go/parser\"\n10|\t\"go/token\"\n11|\t\"os\"\n12|\t\"path/filepath\"\n13|\t\"sort\"\n14|\t\"strconv\"\n15|\t\"strings\"\n16|\t\"testing\"\n17|\t\"time\"\n18|\n19|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/scalar\"\n20|)\n21|\n22|// This file is the derived refusal-arm inventory. It exists because the\n23|// constructor call-site audit in inventory_test.go enumerates constructor\n24|// call SITES, and every frameFault literal and every integrity(...) detail\n25|// funnels through a shared site: planting a new arm through an existing\n26|// site (a new &frameFault literal in checkResponseMembers, a new\n27|// integrity(...) detail in DecodeStatusOutcome) leaves the whole suite\n28|// green. Two review rounds each missed a row by hand, so the arm set is\n29|// derived from production source by parsing it, never by listing it.\n30|//\n31|// Derivation (deriveRefusalArms): every &frameFault{...} literal yields\n32|// frame|<detail>|<member source>; every integrity(...) call with a string\n33|// literal yields integrity|<detail>; the single wrapping site\n34|// integrity(\"status body is \"+fault.detail, ...) expands over the derived\n35|// frame detail set, so each wrapped refusal is its own obligation; every\n36|// rejection branch of parseMajor (a return 0, false) yields\n37|// parse|<enclosing condition source>; every literal first argument to one\n38|// of the six refusal constructors yields ctor|<constructor>|<detail>.\n39|// A non-literal frameFault detail or integrity argument lands as an\n40|// expr:<source> obligation rather than passing silently; a non-literal\n41|// constructor first argument is a fault conduit (fault.detail, a detail\n42|// variable) whose arms are the frame arms above, so it carries no\n43|// separate obligation by design. A missing parseMajor fails the\n44|// derivation outright.\n45|//\n46|// Both directions are checked: TestDerivedRefusalArmsAreAllWitnessed\n47|// (every derived arm carries a witness) and\n48|// TestWitnessedArmsAreAllDerived (every witness names a derived arm, so a\n49|// truncated derivation reddens on the orphaned witnesses instead of\n50|// passing vacuously). TestEveryArmWitnessRefusesAtTheProductionEntry\n51|// drives each witness through the production entry and requires the\n52|// refusal to come from the arm under test. Empty, single-file, or\n53|// unparseable derivations fail closed: a domain that silently derives\n54|// nothing is not a measurement.\n55|//\n56|// Stated bound: arms sharing one (constructor, detail) identity merge to\n57|// one obligation (the two timeout sites, the two empty-response sites,\n58|// the six identical \"not a JSON object\" sites). Deleting one of a merged\n59|// pair is a behavioral mutant the entry-point tests must catch, not this\n60|// inventory.\n61|\n62|// refusalArmCensusFloor is the derived arm count this test was written\n63|// against. It is a tripwire, not an enumeration: a derivation returning\n64|// fewer arms fails closed even when every surviving arm is witnessed,\n65|// which is what catches a silently truncated scan. Raising it is routine\n66|// when production gains a refusal; lowering it requires saying why.\n67|//\n68|// Raised 60 -> 162 by the operation-layer leaf (manifest, probe,\n69|// profile, quiescence, spawn, identity, idempotency decoders), each\n70|// new arm witnessed in declaredOperationWitnesses below, then 162 ->\n71|// 164 by the lone-surrogate gate and 164 -> 166 by the UTF-8 gate:\n72|// one frame arm in decodeStrictObject plus its status-body integrity\n73|// expansion each, every one witnessed above.\n74|const refusalArmCensusFloor = 166\n75|\n76|func deriveRefusalArms(t *testing.T) map[string]struct{} {\n77|\tt.Helper()\n78|\tdirectory, err := os.Getwd()\n79|\tif err != nil {\n80|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"derive refusal arms: %v\", err)\n81|\t}\n82|\tarms, scanned, err := refusalArmsIn(directory)\n83|\tif err != nil {\n84|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"derive refusal arms: %v\", err)\n85|\t}\n86|\tif len(scanned) == 0 {\n87|\t\tt.Fatal(\"derived refusal arms from zero production files; the scanner is broken, not the package\")\n88|\t}\n89|\tif len(arms) == 0 {\n90|\t\tt.Fatal(\"derived zero refusal arms from the package sources; the scanner is broken, not the package\")\n91|\t}\n92|\tif len(arms) < refusalArmCensusFloor {\n93|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"derived %d refusal arms, below the %d census floor; the derivation is short, not the package\", len(arms), refusalArmCensusFloor)\n94|\t}\n95|\tt.Logf(\"refusal arm coverage domain: %d derived arms across %d production files\", len(arms), len(scanned))\n96|\treturn arms\n97|}\n98|\n99|func refusalArmsIn(directory string) (map[string]struct{}, []string, error) {\n100|\tentries, err := os.ReadDir(directory)\n101|\tif err != nil {\n102|\t\treturn nil, nil, err\n103|\t}\n104|\tarms := map[string]struct{}{}\n105|\tvar scanned []string\n106|\tparseBranches := 0\n107|\tfileSet := token.NewFileSet()\n108|\ttype productionFile struct {\n109|\t\tsyntax *ast.File\n110|\t\tsource []byte\n111|\t}\n112|\tvar files []productionFile\n113|\tfor _, entry := range entries {\n114|\t\tname := entry.Name()\n115|\t\tif entry.IsDir() || !strings.HasSuffix(name, \".go\") || strings.HasSuffix(name, \"_test.go\") {\n116|\t\t\tcontinue\n117|\t\t}\n118|\t\tscanned = append(scanned, name)\n119|\t\tpath := filepath.Join(directory, name)\n120|\t\tsource, err := os.ReadFile(path)\n121|\t\tif err != nil {\n122|\t\t\treturn nil, nil, err\n123|\t\t}\n124|\t\tsyntax, err := parser.ParseFile(fileSet, path, source, parser.ParseComments)\n125|\t\tif err != nil {\n126|\t\t\treturn nil, nil, err\n127|\t\t}\n128|\t\tfiles = append(files, productionFile{syntax: syntax, source: source})\n129|\t}\n130|\t// First pass, package-wide: the decodeStrictObject fault detail\n131|\t// set, which the integrity wrapper site expands over. The wrapper\n132|\t// only wraps decodeStrictObject faults, so checkResponseMembers\n133|\t// arms (\"missing member\", \"unknown member\", ...) are not in this\n134|\t// set: expanding over every frameFault literal would invent arms\n135|\t// production can never emit. The pass must span files because the\n136|\t// literals live in protocol.go while the wrapper lives in status.go.\n137|\tvar strictDetails []string\n138|\tseenDetail := map[string]bool{}\n139|\tfor _, file := range files {\n140|\t\tfor _, decl := range file.syntax.Decls {\n141|\t\t\tfunction, ok := decl.(*ast.FuncDecl)\n142|\t\t\tif !ok || function.Name.Name != \"decodeStrictObject\" {\n143|\t\t\t\tcontinue\n144|\t\t\t}\n145|\t\t\tast.Inspect(function.Body, func(node ast.Node) bool {\n146|\t\t\t\tliteral, ok := frameFaultLiteral(node)\n147|\t\t\t\tif !ok {\n148|\t\t\t\t\treturn true\n149|\t\t\t\t}\n150|\t\t\t\tdetail, ok := literalStringField(file.source, fileSet, literal, \"detail\")\n151|\t\t\t\tif !ok {\n152|\t\t\t\t\treturn true\n153|\t\t\t\t}\n154|\t\t\t\tif !seenDetail[detail] {\n155|\t\t\t\t\tseenDetail[detail] = true\n156|\t\t\t\t\tstrictDetails = append(strictDetails, detail)\n157|\t\t\t\t}\n158|\t\t\t\treturn true\n159|\t\t\t})\n160|\t\t}\n161|\t}\n162|\tfor _, file := range files {\n163|\t\tsource, syntax := file.source, file.syntax\n164|\t\tparseBranches += armParseBranches(source, fileSet, syntax, arms)\n165|\t\tast.Inspect(syntax, func(node ast.Node) bool {\n166|\t\t\tif literal, ok := frameFaultLiteral(node); ok {\n167|\t\t\t\tdetail, ok := literalStringField(source, fileSet, literal, \"detail\")\n168|\t\t\t\tif !ok {\n169|\t\t\t\t\tarms[\"frame|expr:\"+nodeSource(source, fileSet, node)] = struct{}{}\n170|\t\t\t\t\treturn true\n171|\t\t\t\t}\n172|\t\t\t\tmember := \"\"\n173|\t\t\t\tif kv := literalField(literal, \"member\"); kv != nil {\n174|\t\t\t\t\tmember = nodeSource(source, fileSet, kv.Value)\n175|\t\t\t\t}\n176|\t\t\t\tarms[\"frame|\"+detail+\"|\"+member] = struct{}{}\n177|\t\t\t\treturn true\n178|\t\t\t}\n179|\t\t\tcall, ok := node.(*ast.CallExpr)\n180|\t\t\tif !ok {\n181|\t\t\t\treturn true\n182|\t\t\t}\n183|\t\t\tident, ok := call.Fun.(*ast.Ident)\n184|\t\t\tif !ok || len(call.Args) == 0 {\n185|\t\t\t\treturn true\n186|\t\t\t}\n187|\t\t\tswitch ident.Name {\n188|\t\t\tcase \"integrity\":\n189|\t\t\t\tif literal, ok := call.Args[0].(*ast.BasicLit); ok && literal.Kind == token.STRING {\n190|\t\t\t\t\tdetail, err := strconv.Unquote(literal.Value)\n191|\t\t\t\t\tif err != nil {\n192|\t\t\t\t\t\tarms[\"integrity|expr:\"+nodeSource(source, fileSet, call.Args[0])] = struct{}{}\n193|\t\t\t\t\t\treturn true\n194|\t\t\t\t\t}\n195|\t\t\t\t\tarms[\"integrity|\"+detail] = struct{}{}\n196|\t\t\t\t\treturn true\n197|\t\t\t\t}\n198|\t\t\t\tif prefix, ok := integrityPrefix(call.Args[0]); ok {\n199|\t\t\t\t\tif len(strictDetails) == 0 {\n200|\t\t\t\t\t\tarms[\"integrity|expr:\"+nodeSource(source, fileSet, call.Args[0])] = struct{}{}\n201|\t\t\t\t\t\treturn true\n202|\t\t\t\t\t}\n203|\t\t\t\t\tfor _, detail := range strictDetails {\n204|\t\t\t\t\t\tarms[\"integrity|\"+prefix+detail] = struct{}{}\n205|\t\t\t\t\t}\n206|\t\t\t\t\treturn true\n207|\t\t\t\t}\n208|\t\t\t\tarms[\"integrity|expr:\"+nodeSource(source, fileSet, call.Args[0])] = struct{}{}\n209|\t\t\tcase \"failInvalid\", \"failProtocol\", \"failMismatch\", \"failProcess\", \"failTimeout\":\n210|\t\t\t\tif literal, ok := call.Args[0].(*ast.BasicLit); ok && literal.Kind == token.STRING {\n211|\t\t\t\t\tdetail, err := strconv.Unquote(literal.Value)\n212|\t\t\t\t\tif err != nil {\n213|\t\t\t\t\t\treturn true\n214|\t\t\t\t\t}\n215|\t\t\t\t\tarms[\"ctor|\"+ident.Name+\"|\"+detail] = struct{}{}\n216|\t\t\t\t}\n217|\t\t\t\t// Non-literal first arguments are the fault conduits\n218|\t\t\t\t// (fault.detail, detail variables): the arms behind\n219|\t\t\t\t// them are the frame arms above, so there is no\n220|\t\t\t\t// separate obligation here.\n221|\t\t\t}\n222|\t\t\treturn true\n223|\t\t})\n224|\t}\n225|\tif parseBranches == 0 {\n226|\t\treturn nil, nil, fmt.Errorf(\"parseMajor carries no rejection branch anywhere; the classification-branch enumeration is blind\")\n227|\t}\n228|\tsort.Strings(scanned)\n229|\treturn arms, scanned, nil\n230|}\n231|\n232|// frameFaultLiteral reports whether node is a &frameFault{...} literal.\n233|func frameFaultLiteral(node ast.Node) (*ast.CompositeLit, bool) {\n234|\ttarget := node\n235|\tif unary, ok := node.(*ast.UnaryExpr); ok && unary.Op == token.AND {\n236|\t\ttarget = unary.X\n237|\t}\n238|\tliteral, ok := target.(*ast.CompositeLit)\n239|\tif !ok {\n240|\t\treturn nil, false\n241|\t}\n242|\tident, ok := literal.Type.(*ast.Ident)\n243|\tif !ok || ident.Name != \"frameFault\" {\n244|\t\treturn nil, false\n245|\t}\n246|\treturn literal, true\n247|}\n248|\n249|func literalField(literal *ast.CompositeLit, name string) *ast.KeyValueExpr {\n250|\tfor _, element := range literal.Elts {\n251|\t\tif kv, ok := element.(*ast.KeyValueExpr); ok {\n252|\t\t\tif ident, ok := kv.Key.(*ast.Ident); ok && ident.Name == name {\n253|\t\t\t\treturn kv\n254|\t\t\t}\n255|\t\t}\n256|\t}\n257|\treturn nil\n258|}\n259|\n260|func literalStringField(source []byte, fileSet *token.FileSet, literal *ast.CompositeLit, name string) (string, bool) {\n261|\tkv := literalField(literal, name)\n262|\tif kv == nil {\n263|\t\treturn \"\", false\n264|\t}\n265|\tbasic, ok := kv.Value.(*ast.BasicLit)\n266|\tif !ok || basic.Kind != token.STRING {\n267|\t\treturn \"\", false\n268|\t}\n269|\tdetail, err := strconv.Unquote(basic.Value)\n270|\tif err != nil {\n271|\t\treturn \"\", false\n272|\t}\n273|\treturn detail, true\n274|}\n275|\n276|// integrityPrefix matches \"prefix\" + <expr>, the wrapping shape whose\n277|// arms expand over the derived frame detail set.\n278|func integrityPrefix(arg ast.Expr) (string, bool) {\n279|\tbinary, ok := arg.(*ast.BinaryExpr)\n280|\tif !ok || binary.Op != token.ADD {\n281|\t\treturn \"\", false\n282|\t}\n283|\tprefix, ok := binary.X.(*ast.BasicLit)\n284|\tif !ok || prefix.Kind != token.STRING {\n285|\t\treturn \"\", false\n286|\t}\n287|\ttext, err := strconv.Unquote(prefix.Value)\n288|\tif err != nil {\n289|\t\treturn \"\", false\n290|\t}\n291|\treturn text, true\n292|}\n293|\n294|func nodeSource(source []byte, fileSet *token.FileSet, node ast.Node) string {\n295|\tstart := fileSet.Position(node.Pos()).Offset\n296|\tend := fileSet.Position(node.End()).Offset\n297|\tif start < 0 || end > len(source) || start >= end {\n298|\t\treturn \"?\"\n299|\t}\n300|\treturn strings.Join(strings.Fields(string(source[start:end])), \" \")\n301|}\n302|\n303|// armParseBranches derives one obligation per parseMajor rejection\n304|// branch in this file: every return 0, false inside parseMajor, keyed by\n305|// its innermost enclosing condition, and returns how many it derived. A\n306|// new branch adds a key no witness names; a deleted branch orphans its\n307|// witness; narrowing || to && rewrites the key and does both. The caller\n308|// fails closed when no file derives any branch.\n309|func armParseBranches(source []byte, fileSet *token.FileSet, syntax *ast.File, arms map[string]struct{}) int {\n310|\tvar body *ast.BlockStmt\n311|\tfor _, decl := range syntax.Decls {\n312|\t\tfunction, ok := decl.(*ast.FuncDecl)\n313|\t\tif ok && function.Name.Name == \"parseMajor\" {\n314|\t\t\tbody = function.Body\n315|\t\t}\n316|\t}\n317|\tif body == nil {\n318|\t\treturn 0\n319|\t}\n320|\tcount := 0\n321|\tvar conditions []string\n322|\tvar walk func(node ast.Node)\n323|\twalk = func(node ast.Node) {\n324|\t\tbranch, ok := node.(*ast.IfStmt)\n325|\t\tif !ok {\n326|\t\t\tfor _, child := range childNodes(node) {\n327|\t\t\t\twalk(child)\n328|\t\t\t}\n329|\t\t\treturn\n330|\t\t}\n331|\t\tconditions = append(conditions, nodeSource(source, fileSet, branch.Cond))\n332|\t\tfor _, stmt := range branch.Body.List {\n333|\t\t\tif ret, ok := stmt.(*ast.ReturnStmt); ok && isFalsePair(ret) {\n334|\t\t\t\tarms[\"parse|\"+conditions[len(conditions)-1]] = struct{}{}\n335|\t\t\t\tcount++\n336|\t\t\t}\n337|\t\t}\n338|\t\tfor _, child := range childNodes(node) {\n339|\t\t\twalk(child)\n340|\t\t}\n341|\t\tconditions = conditions[:len(conditions)-1]\n342|\t}\n343|\twalk(body)\n344|\treturn count\n345|}\n346|\n347|func isFalsePair(ret *ast.ReturnStmt) bool {\n348|\tif len(ret.Results) != 2 {\n349|\t\treturn false\n350|\t}\n351|\tzero, ok := ret.Results[0].(*ast.BasicLit)\n352|\tif !ok || zero.Kind != token.INT || zero.Value != \"0\" {\n353|\t\treturn false\n354|\t}\n355|\tno, ok := ret.Results[1].(*ast.Ident)\n356|\treturn ok && no.Name == \"false\"\n357|}\n358|\n359|func childNodes(node ast.Node) []ast.Node {\n360|\tvar children []ast.Node\n361|\tast.Inspect(node, func(child ast.Node) bool {\n362|\t\tif child == nil || child == node {\n363|\t\t\treturn true\n364|\t\t}\n365|\t\tchildren = append(children, child)\n366|\t\treturn false\n367|\t})\n368|\treturn children\n369|}\n370|\n371|// armWitness proves one derived refusal arm at the production entry.\n372|// The arm key must equal the derived key exactly: TestWitnessedArmsAreAllDerived\n373|// fails a witness that names nothing production declares, so a deleted or\n374|// narrowed production branch orphans its witness instead of passing\n375|// silently. The prove function must drive the production entry point and\n376|// require the refusal attributed to THIS arm, not merely any refusal.\n377|type armWitness struct {\n378|\tarm   string\n379|\tname  string\n380|\tprove func(*testing.T)\n381|}\n382|\n383|// requireIntegrityRefusal asserts the full identity of a status refusal:\n384|// the integrity_failure code, the rule detail, the status_state detail\n385|// every integrity arm carries (AS6: asserted on all 18 arms, not just\n386|// the unknown row), exit 9, and the non-retryable bit. It is separate\n387|// from requireLocalRefusal because that helper also serves codes with no\n388|// status_state detail.\n389|func requireIntegrityRefusal(t *testing.T, err error, detail, wantState string) {\n390|\tt.Helper()\n391|\trequireLocalRefusal(t, err, \"integrity_failure\", detail)\n392|\tstate, ok := failureObject(t, err).Detail(\"status_state\")\n393|\tif !ok || state != wantState {\n394|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"integrity refusal status_state = %v, want %q (%v)\", state, wantState, err)\n395|\t}\n396|\tif failureExit(t, err) != 9 {\n397|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"integrity refusal exit = %d, want 9\", failureExit(t, err))\n398|\t}\n399|}\n400|\n401|func armVersionFrame(version string) []byte {\n402|\treturn []byte(`{\"protocol\":\"urn:ax:protocol:provider\",\"protocol_version\":\"` + version + `\",\"request_id\":\"` + testRequestID + `\",\"ok\":true,\"body\":{}}`)\n403|}\n404|\n405|func armMemberFrame(members string) []byte {\n406|\treturn []byte(`{\"protocol\":\"urn:ax:protocol:provider\",\"protocol_version\":\"2.0.0\",\"request_id\":\"` + testRequestID + `\",` + members + `}`)\n407|}\n408|\n409|func armOversizeResponse(t *testing.T) []byte {\n410|\tt.Helper()\n411|\tbuild := func(pad int) []byte {\n412|\t\treturn successFrame(t, testRequestID, `{\"pad\":\"`+strings.Repeat(\"a\", pad)+`\"}`)\n413|\t}\n414|\tbase := len(build(0))\n415|\tover := build(specFrameLimitBytes - base + 1)\n416|\tif len(over) != specFrameLimitBytes+1 {\n417|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"oversize fixture is %d bytes, want exactly %d\", len(over), specFrameLimitBytes+1)\n418|\t}\n419|\treturn over\n420|}\n421|\n422|func declaredArmWitnesses() []armWitness {\n423|\treturn []armWitness{\n424|\t\t// decodeStrictObject frame arms, through DecodeResponse.\n425|\t\t{arm: `frame|not a JSON object|\"\"`, name: \"array is not an object\", prove: func(t *testing.T) {\n426|\t\t\t_, err := DecodeResponse([]byte(`[1,2]`), mustUUIDv7(t, testRequestID))\n427|\t\t\trequireFrameRefusal(t, err, \"\", \"not a JSON object\")\n428|\t\t}},\n429|\t\t{arm: `frame|not a JSON object|key`, name: \"truncated value names its member\", prove: func(t *testing.T) {\n430|\t\t\t_, err := DecodeResponse([]byte(`{\"protocol\":`), mustUUIDv7(t, testRequestID))\n431|\t\t\trequireFrameRefusal(t, err, \"protocol\", \"not a JSON object\")\n432|\t\t}},\n433|\t\t{arm: `frame|duplicate member|key`, name: \"repeated member\", prove: func(t *testing.T) {\n434|\t\t\tframe := []byte(`{\"protocol\":\"urn:ax:protocol:provider\",\"protocol_version\":\"2.0.0\",\"request_id\":\"` + testRequestID + `\",\"request_id\":\"` + testRequestID + `\",\"ok\":true,\"body\":{}}`)\n435|\t\t\t_, err := DecodeResponse(frame, mustUUIDv7(t, testRequestID))\n436|\t\t\trequireFrameRefusal(t, err, \"request_id\", \"duplicate member\")\n437|\t\t}},\n438|\t\t{arm: `frame|trailing data after the object|\"\"`, name: \"trailing byte\", prove: func(t *testing.T) {\n439|\t\t\t_, err := DecodeResponse(append(successFrame(t, testRequestID, `{\"provider_id\":\"pi\"}`), 'x'), mustUUIDv7(t, testRequestID))\n440|\t\t\trequireFrameRefusal(t, err, \"\", \"trailing data after the object\")\n441|\t\t}},\n442|\t\t{arm: `frame|lone surrogate escape|\"\"`, name: \"lone surrogate in body\", prove: func(t *testing.T) {\n443|\t\t\t_, err := DecodeResponse(successFrame(t, testRequestID, `{\"provider_id\":\"pi\",\"tag\":\"a\\ud800b\"}`), mustUUIDv7(t, testRequestID))\n444|\t\t\trequireFrameRefusal(t, err, \"\", \"lone surrogate escape\")\n445|\t\t}},\n446|\t\t{arm: `frame|not valid UTF-8|\"\"`, name: \"raw bytes in body\", prove: func(t *testing.T) {\n447|\t\t\terr := DecodeManifest([]byte(\"{\\\"note\\\":\\\"ab\\xffcd\\\"}\"))\n448|\t\t\trequireFrameRefusal(t, err, \"\", \"not valid UTF-8\")\n449|\t\t}},\n450|\t\t{arm: `frame|missing member|name`, name: \"missing protocol\", prove: func(t *testing.T) {\n451|\t\t\tframe := []byte(`{\"protocol_version\":\"2.0.0\",\"request_id\":\"` + testRequestID + `\",\"ok\":true,\"body\":{}}`)\n452|\t\t\t_, err := DecodeResponse(frame, mustUUIDv7(t, testRequestID))\n453|\t\t\trequireFrameRefusal(t, err, \"protocol\", \"missing member\")\n454|\t\t}},\n455|\t\t{arm: `frame|missing member|\"body\"`, name: \"success without body\", prove: func(t *testing.T) {\n456|\t\t\t_, err := DecodeResponse(armMemberFrame(`\"ok\":true`), mustUUIDv7(t, testRequestID))\n457|\t\t\trequireFrameRefusal(t, err, \"body\", \"missing member\")\n458|\t\t}},\n459|\t\t{arm: `frame|success envelope carries error|\"error\"`, name: \"error on success\", prove: func(t *testing.T) {\n460|\t\t\tframe := []byte(`{\"protocol\":\"urn:ax:protocol:provider\",\"protocol_version\":\"2.0.0\",\"request_id\":\"` + testRequestID + `\",\"ok\":true,\"body\":{},\"error\":{\"schema\":\"urn:ax:schema:error\",\"schema_version\":\"1.0.0\",\"code\":\"capability_unavailable\",\"message\":\"m\",\"exit_code\":6,\"retryable\":false,\"details\":{}}}`)\n461|\t\t\t_, err := DecodeResponse(frame, mustUUIDv7(t, testRequestID))\n462|\t\t\trequireFrameRefusal(t, err, \"error\", \"success envelope carries error\")\n463|\t\t}},\n464|\t\t{arm: `frame|missing member|\"error\"`, name: \"failure without error\", prove: func(t *testing.T) {\n465|\t\t\t_, err := DecodeResponse(armMemberFrame(`\"ok\":false`), mustUUIDv7(t, testRequestID))\n466|\t\t\trequireFrameRefusal(t, err, \"error\", \"missing member\")\n467|\t\t}},\n468|\t\t{arm: `frame|failure envelope carries body|\"body\"`, name: \"body on failure\", prove: func(t *testing.T) {\n469|\t\t\tframe := []byte(`{\"protocol\":\"urn:ax:protocol:provider\",\"protocol_version\":\"2.0.0\",\"request_id\":\"` + testRequestID + `\",\"ok\":false,\"error\":{\"schema\":\"urn:ax:schema:error\",\"schema_version\":\"1.0.0\",\"code\":\"capability_unavailable\",\"message\":\"m\",\"exit_code\":6,\"retryable\":false,\"details\":{}},\"body\":{}}`)\n470|\t\t\t_, err := DecodeResponse(frame, mustUUIDv7(t, testRequestID))\n471|\t\t\trequireFrameRefusal(t, err, \"body\", \"failure envelope carries body\")\n472|\t\t}},\n473|\t\t{arm: `frame|unknown member|name`, name: \"diagnostics member\", prove: func(t *testing.T) {\n474|\t\t\t_, err := DecodeResponse(armMemberFrame(`\"ok\":true,\"body\":{},\"diagnostics\":[]`), mustUUIDv7(t, testRequestID))\n475|\t\t\trequireFrameRefusal(t, err, \"diagnostics\", \"unknown member\")\n476|\t\t}},\n477|\t\t// encodeFrame refusals, through EncodeRequest.\n478|\t\t{arm: `ctor|failInvalid|unknown operation`, name: \"unknown operation never frames\", prove: func(t *testing.T) {\n479|\t\t\treq := testRequest(t)\n480|\t\t\treq.Operation = \"reboot\"\n481|\t\t\t_, err := EncodeRequest(req, mustInstant(t, testNow))\n482|\t\t\trequireLocalRefusal(t, err, \"invalid_config\", \"unknown operation\")\n483|\t\t}},\n484|\t\t{arm: `ctor|failInvalid|request_id is not a UUIDv7`, name: \"zero request id\", prove: func(t *testing.T) {\n485|\t\t\tbad := testRequest(t)\n486|\t\t\tvar zero scalar.UUIDv7\n487|\t\t\tbad.RequestID = zero\n488|\t\t\t_, err := EncodeRequest(bad, mustInstant(t, testNow))\n489|\t\t\trequireLocalRefusal(t, err, \"invalid_config\", \"request_id is not a UUIDv7\")\n490|\t\t}},\n491|\t\t{arm: `ctor|failInvalid|deadline is not a timestamp`, name: \"zero deadline\", prove: func(t *testing.T) {\n492|\t\t\treq := testRequest(t)\n493|\t\t\treq.Deadline = mustTimestamp(t, testDeadline)\n494|\t\t\tvar zero scalar.Timestamp\n495|\t\t\treq.Deadline = zero\n496|\t\t\t_, err := EncodeRequest(req, mustInstant(t, testNow))\n497|\t\t\trequireLocalRefusal(t, err, \"invalid_config\", \"deadline is not a timestamp\")\n498|\t\t}},\n499|\t\t{arm: `ctor|failInvalid|deadline is not in the future`, name: \"stale deadline\", prove: func(t *testing.T) {\n500|\t\t\treq := testRequest(t)\n(more lines below)"}}}
